#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179582 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "2574b91a-6534-562b-b4dc-8d95fd19e169" :question/math-academy-id "e-9480" :question/problem "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =Δ{y}_{1}+Δ{y}_{2}+Δ{y}_{3}+⋯+Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179583 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "8f09771b-3e0d-567b-a39f-f877bff53372" :question/math-academy-id "e-9481" :question/problem "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179585 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "eff8c72f-429d-583a-aa22-f7786f09262a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9484" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]?$\n\nI. $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n\nII. $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n\nIII. $1 <     2  <    9$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efe5619c-047f-57cf-a68b-6582ef36b805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177538} {:answer/id #uuid "0809d7b1-2306-5988-a232-bb9ecc7c8380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177539} {:answer/id #uuid "0b3c366a-1c39-520e-8fe5-b79341d95e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177540} {:answer/id #uuid "0f2090ea-3a96-53fa-9848-51207528b6e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177541} {:answer/id #uuid "4a93998e-0289-52f9-9819-d775a1577621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177542}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8ecfdc2d-9d95-5ab8-8261-61743a106817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177537}] :question/id #uuid "e015992d-dc19-5c46-a968-6f970052cd44" :question/math-academy-id "q-122864" :question/problem "Let $P = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0, 4]$. If $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, calculate $∑_(j = 1)^(n)8(y_{j} + y_{j - 1})Δy_{j}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a3bc488-a654-58e2-acea-0cde8ca417ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177550} {:answer/id #uuid "add59b06-7aff-5f7b-8180-26392d448211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177551} {:answer/id #uuid "b786bbfd-7079-5e8f-98c4-4aeea35947a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177552} {:answer/id #uuid "5668f2db-b736-55e7-ba82-255e5d7afa67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[- 2, 6]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177553} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd66c47-0f50-5072-838a-2f9ab0170ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177554}] :answer-field/id #uuid "aced8254-1be3-536c-8537-7e94eb28d2e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177549}] :question/id #uuid "0668e0bd-4637-511c-a263-1fb809d9cda4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122923" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[- 2, 6]$?\n\n1. ${-2,-1, 0, 6}$\n2. ${0, 2, 4, 6}$\n3. $-2 < 2 < 4 < 5$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4650d883-0024-5fb8-8a3b-926b85faeb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523398} {:answer/id #uuid "91e31bb5-4dda-578c-be6e-626d6d5b43b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523560} {:answer/id #uuid "962aff86-8fb7-5334-ab89-1ce