b/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b01046-18e1-58bb-9aae-addee4a5482b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523302} {:answer/id #uuid "79640bcf-217a-5e27-aca2-3c90383899ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523502} {:answer/id #uuid "84c6b261-478a-5a3c-8af3-eb635d34e070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523534} {:answer/id #uuid "9e84a909-3d25-5602-9873-2133f303f3b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[0,6]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523585} {:answer/id #uuid "cc89bb28-0e81-56bc-b07d-003f53e45ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15b01046-18e1-58bb-9aae-addee4a5482b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523302} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b6f0340-20ad-55e8-b95b-71619bc5062f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e49f5076-911d-5cdf-8140-a000de972953" :question/math-academy-id "q-122934" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,6]?$\n\nI. $0<2<4<8$\n\nII. $\\{0,3,6\\}$\n\nIII. $0<1<3<5<6$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,6]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbdbd0b-c1a2-51c0-a8f5-15cb04158568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523478} {:answer/id #uuid "929a1813-87ee-5a94-b302-53b3394322ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523562} {:answer/id #uuid "960de9e7-c3d1-548d-bb28-aea79c7b0d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523569} {:answer/id #uuid "d15c5ee3-1df2-5a89-801e-42aef64a0cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523696} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c61e9b-6f94-5835-aa08-0cb0ef8d2485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbdbd0b-c1a2-51c0-a8f5-15cb04158568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523478} :answer-field/id #uuid "da6d1a46-d11c-5863-8635-3e515e9d04b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28824d9b-0c0b-596c-9f64-75c745081e48" :question/math-academy-id "q-122969" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,8].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,8],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =8-2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07195f6c-4e48-5dcc-aec2-5d69c56026d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523272} {:answer/id #uuid "5665712a-009d-5af0-a804-20166b15f257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523431} {:answer/id #uuid "916a6352-92eb-5096-b435-cd193b6feb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523558} {:answer/id #uuid "f878e57d-c65e-5d5e-8918-ff905b1034b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523775} {:answer/id #uuid "ff90e828-6c3f-5567-ad48-f5f15d008572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07195f6c-4e48-5dcc-aec2-5d69c56026d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523272} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee43f80-f80a-52f4-830f-025c4b4ca95b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1ddbd77-4be4-59b3-aa0d-217f8714ae20" :question/math-academy-id "q-122971" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-5,5].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[-5,5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-5) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "154c6ccd-afa9-5d6e-b30d-795512a973b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523300} {:answer/id #uuid "3e17c7a9-6c99-5817-8972-75e58e23f040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "190" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523385} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa8eabe-8df9-5652-9574-6fce6e9ce159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "196" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523387} {:answer/id #uuid "a8cc2c6a-d627-5733-9397-df08623f6047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523611} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c1fe78-e46c-5dc7-811d-7c100ded5e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "198" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8c1fe78-e46c-5dc7-811d-7c100ded5e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "198" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523777} :answer-field/id #uuid "df659612-579e-586d-b30d-ba9a4e631fa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "785f4fec-653e-532c-a878-3835d225527c" :question/math-academy-id "q-122994" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[1,10].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}2({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}2({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=1$ and ${x}_{m}=10$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={10}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =99.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=2\\cdot 99=198.\n$$"}]}
